{"3811500":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"The Curse of Ooty","steam_appid":3811500,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"detailed_description":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >She was fine when you left the city.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >You picked her up for the drive to Ooty. Somewhere on the road into the Nilgiris, something followed her into the car.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >By the time you arrive she is not herself. A stray dog leads you through the dark to an aghori who keeps a fire burning at the edge of the village. He knows what has her. He will give her back — but first you bring him what he asks for.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >One lantern. One night. A list you did not write.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >• Carry a kerosene lantern that lights a few feet of ground and nothing past it.<br>• Navigate by compass through fog, groves and unlit village lanes.<br>• Search a lake boat, an abandoned railway station and a house full of puppets for what the aghori needs.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Every door has a ritual behind it.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >• Align occult dials to open what somebody sealed.<br>• Rebuild torn family portraits to learn who lived here, and who did not.<br>• Light shrine offerings in the right order while something moves outside.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Speak carefully.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >• The aghori answers what you ask, in the way you ask it.<br>• Dialogue choices decide what you learn about the thing holding her.<br>• What you learn changes what it learns about you.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Things that are already awake.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >• A doll that follows you between the huts.<br>• A child trailing a red balloon through the fog.<br>• Twin spirits in red saris that will not stop screaming.<br>• And at the end of the aghori's list, the snake.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Set in a place, not a backdrop.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Ooty, in the Nilgiri hills of southern India. Tamil station signage, mud-brick homes, kerosene light, village shrines and aghori fire. Rahasya is built on Indian folk ritual rather than borrowed ghosts.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Dialogue and subtitles in Hindi.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >You drove her here. Drive back with her, or do not drive back.<\/h2>","about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >She was fine when you left the city.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >You picked her up for the drive to Ooty. Somewhere on the road into the Nilgiris, something followed her into the car.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >By the time you arrive she is not herself. A stray dog leads you through the dark to an aghori who keeps a fire burning at the edge of the village. He knows what has her. He will give her back — but first you bring him what he asks for.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >One lantern. One night. A list you did not write.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >• Carry a kerosene lantern that lights a few feet of ground and nothing past it.<br>• Navigate by compass through fog, groves and unlit village lanes.<br>• Search a lake boat, an abandoned railway station and a house full of puppets for what the aghori needs.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Every door has a ritual behind it.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >• Align occult dials to open what somebody sealed.<br>• Rebuild torn family portraits to learn who lived here, and who did not.<br>• Light shrine offerings in the right order while something moves outside.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Speak carefully.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >• The aghori answers what you ask, in the way you ask it.<br>• Dialogue choices decide what you learn about the thing holding her.<br>• What you learn changes what it learns about you.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Things that are already awake.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >• A doll that follows you between the huts.<br>• A child trailing a red balloon through the fog.<br>• Twin spirits in red saris that will not stop screaming.<br>• And at the end of the aghori's list, the snake.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Set in a place, not a backdrop.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Ooty, in the Nilgiri hills of southern India. Tamil station signage, mud-brick homes, kerosene light, village shrines and aghori fire. Rahasya is built on Indian folk ritual rather than borrowed ghosts.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Dialogue and subtitles in Hindi.<\/h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >You drove her here. Drive back with her, or do not drive back.<\/h2>","short_description":"You drove her from the city to Ooty. Something followed her into the car. Now she is possessed, and an aghori in the hills will only help if you bring him what he asks for. First-person Indian folk horror.","supported_languages":"English, Hindi, Spanish - Spain, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese - Brazil, Russian, Simplified Chinese, Turkish","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3811500\/999cbc2be0310755d8cb01641f143abc0ec8b841\/header.jpg?t=1793640506","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3811500\/0bc11d6d0dad0bc244bfc760bac369ce22eaa20c\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793640506","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3811500\/0bc11d6d0dad0bc244bfc760bac369ce22eaa20c\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793640506","website":"https:\/\/abhaykumarr.github.io\/The-Curse-Of-OOTY\/","pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 10 (64-bit<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Intel Core i5 \/ AMD Ryzen 5<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 16 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060<br><\/li><li><strong>DirectX:<\/strong> Version 11<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 8 GB available space<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> 64-bit Windows only. Headphones recommended<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong